            "title": "RWE CEO sees no need for writedowns on major US offshore project",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "DUESSELDORF (Reuters) -RWE, the world's No. 2 developer of offshore wind, sees no need to write down a 3-gigawatt project in the United States, its CEO said, just days after the U.S. government ordered bigger rival Orsted to stop construction on an advanced site.  The so-called Community Offshore Wind project, which RWE owns in a 73%-27% ownership split with Britain's National Grid, has been put on ice and no investment decision has been taken, Markus Krebber told journalists.  Offshore wind has been in the crosshairs of U.S. President Donald Trump, whose administration has taken several steps to halt or prevent construction of projects off the U.S. coast.",
